# Vue / TypeScript Modularity

## File size limits

- Vue SFC components: **≤ 200 lines** per file
- Composables / utils / types modules: **≤ 150 lines** per file
- If a file grows past its limit, split by responsibility before adding more code

## Layer ownership

| Area | Owns |
|------|------|
| `src/types/` | Public TypeScript contract only |
| `src/components/` | Declarative SVG/Vue rendering |
| `src/composables/` | Reactive derivation (scales, viewport, tails, labels, hover) |
| `src/utils/` | Pure helpers (no Vue reactivity, no DOM) |
| `demo/` | Playground app + mocks — not shipped in `dist/` |
| `spikes/` | Throwaway prototypes — not production API |

## Responsibility rules

- **Vue owns the DOM. D3 provides math only** (scales, ticks, paths) — never D3 DOM selection/mutation
- **One primary responsibility per module.** If a composable both layouts labels *and* owns hover state, split it
- **No host-application types** in the public API (`AppState`, app stores, etc.)
- **Renderer only** — no price fetch, no RRG calculation, no caching

## Review checklist

- Does any file exceed the size limits?
- Are new types in the wrong layer?
- Is D3 used for DOM instead of math?
- Did production code land without Vitest coverage?
